000 #edb/ref 17592186388448 13194139536197 true] [17592186388447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388449 13194139536197 true] [17592186388447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388450 13194139536197 true] [17592186388447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388451 13194139536197 true] [17592186388447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388452 13194139536197 true] [17592186388447 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536197 true] [17592186388447 1041 "selection" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388447 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388450 13194139536197 true] [17592186388447 1110 #uuid "7728e383-2210-54a0-8958-18e81efc881e" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388448 1034 "{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-5x{y}^{′}+6y=0" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388448 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536197 true] [17592186388448 1111 #uuid "cb07061d-f07f-57a7-b984-fc5ffa94b82b" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388449 1034 "x{y}^{″}-5{y}^{′}+\\frac{8}{x}y=0" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536197 true] [17592186388449 1111 #uuid "75df4b17-8fa6-5d19-9812-cee28dfc3fda" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388450 1034 "{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-5x{y}^{′}+8y=0" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536197 true] [17592186388450 1111 #uuid "548bd94c-48ae-5ae4-be8d-7e95925d3eda" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388451 1034 "{y}^{″}-\\frac{5}{x}{y}^{′}+\\frac{8}{x}y=\\frac{2}{x}" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388451 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536197 true] [17592186388451 1111 #uuid "fb3f8868-ba58-51d4-a693-416e3f199152" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388452 1034 "{y}^{″}-5{y}^{′}+8y=x" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388452 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536197 true] [17592186388452 1111 #uuid "434985a7-97b1-5e4a-8571-30c168cb53d3" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388453 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388454 13194139536197 true] [17592186388453 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388457 13194139536197 true] [17592186388453 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388460 13194139536197 true] [17592186388453 1089 "q-338023" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388453 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536197 true] [17592186388453 1100 "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+xy-{e}^{x}=0$ is {{field-3}}." 13194139536197 true] [17592186388453 1113 #uuid "0dc4a39a-133c-5d88-913a-6b2fafc59819" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388453 1145 "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy-{e}^{x}=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)={e}^{x},$ which is different from zero." 13194139536197 true] [17592186388454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388455 13194139536197 true] [17592186388454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388456 13194139536197 true] [17592186388454 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139536197 true] [17592186388454 1041 "field-1" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388454 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388456 13194139536197 true] [17592186388454 1110 #uuid "f33760c5-1d2c-5b3d-a842-a65848ab0494" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388455 1034 "homogeneous" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388455 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536197 true] [17592186388455 1111 #uuid "55ad6cc1-