8 13194139536197 true] [17592186388487 1089 "q-65009" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388487 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536197 true] [17592186388487 1100 "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- ${e}^{x}{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}$\n- $y{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x$\n- $3{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+4{y}^{2}=x$" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388487 1113 #uuid "475611da-016f-5cb2-8388-61fb23e081e1" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388487 1145 "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)={e}^{x},b(x)=0,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\ny{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n3{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+4{y}^{2}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $4{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388489 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388490 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388491 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388492 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388493 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1041 "selection" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388491 13194139536197 true] [17592186388488 1110 #uuid "5297bffe-01e4-5540-805b-2cfd507c3611" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388489 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388489 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536197 true] [17592186388489 1111 #uuid "03b3c576-b762-562b-99cd-9c3ba02ccc37" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388490 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536197 true] [17592186388490 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139